To implement a text editor with multiple text lists (or areas) using Angular, you can follow these steps:

1. **Set up your Angular project**: If you haven't already set up an Angular project, do so using `ng new` or any other method.

2. **Create the main component**: Create a new Angular component where you'll manage the text editor and the text lists.

3. **Use Angular Material for UI elements**: For better user experience, consider using Angular Material components like `mat-form-field`, `mat-list`, etc.

4. **Create a Text Editor Service**: This service will handle the logic of editing the text content.

5. **Implement the Main Component**: In this component, you'll have a text area (`<mat-form-field>`), which will serve as the main text editor, and several `<mat-list>`s that will hold the text lists.

6. **Handle List Selection and Editing**: When selecting a list item, update its content in the main text area and vice versa.

Here's a basic example to get you started:

### Step 1: Set up the Angular Project

```bash
ng new my-text-editor-app
cd my-text-editor-app
```

### Step 2: Install Angular Material if not already installed

```bash
npm install @angular/material --save
```

Add `@angular/material` to your `package.json` under `"devDependencies"`.

### Step 3: Create the Main Component

```bash
ng generate component editor
```

Navigate into the newly generated folder:

```bash
cd editor
```

### Step 4: Implement the Text Editor Service

In `editor.component.ts`, define a service that handles text editing:

```typescript
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root'
})
export class TextEditorService {
  private text = '';

  constructor() {}

  getText(): string {
    return this.text;
  }

  setText(text: string): void {
    this.text = text;
  }
}
```

### Step 5: Implement the Main Component

In `editor.component.html`, add the form field for the text editor:

```html
<form [formGroup]="editorForm" novalidate>
  <mat-form-field appearance="outline">
    <input matInput placeholder="Text here" [(ngModel)]="text" formControlName="content" />
  </mat-form-field>
</form>

<!-- Add multiple <mat-list> elements -->
<ul>
  <!-- Example List Item -->
  <li matListItem>
    <p matListLabel>{{ selectedListItem }}</p>
    <button matButton (click)="editListItem()">Edit</button>
  </li>
  <!-- Repeat this pattern for each list item -->
</ul>
```

